From abb5cb04baabc97261e82653633388ca5a1c028d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:21:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 125/125] net: sparx5: do not double tag frames from the CPU on
 trunk ports

A frame the CPU sends out a VLAN-aware bridge port without an untagged
VLAN leaves the switch with two tags, an outer one with VID 0 around the
frame's own:

  802.1Q vlan 0, 802.1Q vlan 55, ARP who-has 10.0.1.2

The CPU injects frames with their VLAN tag in the frame and VID 0 in
the frame header, and the rewriter on such a port tags every frame,
VID 0 included.  A VLAN interface on the bridge cannot reach anything
over a trunk.

Tag all frames except VID 0 instead.  Frames forwarded by the switch
are always classified to a VLAN in a VLAN-aware bridge, so they are
still tagged.

Signed-off-by: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_vlan.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_vlan.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_vlan.c
index c12e90f7a4ee..55dd02b53d01 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_vlan.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_vlan.c
@@ -249,7 +249,10 @@ void sparx5_vlan_port_apply(struct sparx5 *sparx5,
 			/* Tag all frames except when VID == DEFAULT_VLAN */
 			val |= REW_TAG_CTRL_TAG_CFG_SET(1);
 		else
-			val |= REW_TAG_CTRL_TAG_CFG_SET(3);
+			/* Tag all frames except when VID == 0, frames from
+			 * the CPU carry their own tag and have VID 0.
+			 */
+			val |= REW_TAG_CTRL_TAG_CFG_SET(2);
 	}
 	spx5_wr(val, sparx5, REW_TAG_CTRL(port->portno));
 
